            <ArticleTitle>[Antibodies to Chlamydia pneumoniae in blood serum of patients with ischemic heart disease and presence of complicated lesions in coronary arteries].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Levels of IgM, IgG and IgA antibodies to Chlamydia pneumoniae were measured in 107 patients (age 33-75 years) with documented coronary atherosclerosis and 39 subjects with intact coronary arteries. Rates of seropositivity to C. pneumoniae were 77.6 and 25.6% in patients and &quot;healthy&quot; subjects, respectively (p&lt;0.05). Seropositive (n=83) compared with seronegative (n=24) patients had higher prevalence of complicated lesions (p&lt;0.05).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
